al point in the study of prehistoric cultures in Europe, as it reveals insights into social organization, trade networks, and technological advancements of ancient peoples. Key archaeological findings, including pottery and tools, illuminate the daily lives of its inhabitants, reflecting broader trends in human development during this era.

